Feature: App navigation via touch # features/app/app_navigation.feature:1
  As a user
  I want touch to switch apps
  So I can move between screens easily
  Background:   # features/app/app_navigation.feature:6

  @app @nav
  Scenario: Default app is Energy   # features/app/app_navigation.feature:11
    Given the system is ACTIVE      # features/steps/app_steps.py:9
    And the active app is "Energy"  # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the device is reset       # features/steps/app_steps.py:114
    Then the active app is "Energy" # features/steps/app_steps.py:55

  @app @nav
  Scenario: Touch switches to next app  # features/app/app_navigation.feature:16
    Given the system is ACTIVE          # features/steps/app_steps.py:9
    And the active app is "Energy"      # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    When I tap the screen               # features/steps/app_steps.py:40
    Then the active app is "Clock"      # features/steps/app_steps.py:55

  @app @nav
  Scenario: Frequent taps wrap to the beginning  # features/app/app_navigation.feature:21
    Given the system is ACTIVE                   # features/steps/app_steps.py:9
    And the active app is "Energy"               # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the active app is "Weather"            # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    When I tap the screen                        # features/steps/app_steps.py:40
    Then the active app is "Energy"              # features/steps/app_steps.py:55

  @app @nav @wakeup
  Scenario: Touch wakes device but does not switch apps  # features/app/app_navigation.feature:27
    Given the system is ACTIVE                           # features/steps/app_steps.py:9
    And the active app is "Energy"                       # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the system is IDLE with backlight off          # features/steps/app_steps.py:15
    When I tap the screen                                # features/steps/app_steps.py:40
    Then the system is ACTIVE                            # features/steps/app_steps.py:67
    And the active app is "Energy"                       # features/steps/app_steps.py:55

Feature: Per-app rotary behavior # features/app/app_rotary.feature:1
  As a user
  I want the rotary to control the current app
  So I can change in-app modes without affecting others
  Background:   # features/app/app_rotary.feature:6

  @app @rotary
  Scenario: Rotary affects only the active app  # features/app/app_rotary.feature:10
    Given the active app is "Energy"            # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the Energy mode is "kWh Today"        # features/steps/app_steps.py:97
    When I rotate the encoder RIGHT             # features/steps/app_steps.py:47
    Then the Energy mode becomes the next mode  # features/steps/app_steps.py:97
    And no other app receives the encoder event # features/steps/app_steps.py:105

  @app @rotary
  Scenario: Rotary LEFT cycles modes backwards  # features/app/app_rotary.feature:17
    Given the active app is "Energy"            # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the active app is "Energy"            # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the Energy mode is "kWh Today"        # features/steps/app_steps.py:97
    When I rotate the encoder LEFT              # features/steps/app_steps.py:47
    Then the Energy mode becomes the next mode  # features/steps/app_steps.py:97

  @app @rotary @wakeup
  Scenario: Rotary wakes first, acts second    # features/app/app_rotary.feature:24
    Given the active app is "Energy"           # features/steps/app_steps.py:22
    Given the system is IDLE                   # features/steps/app_steps.py:15
    When I rotate the encoder RIGHT            # features/steps/app_steps.py:47
    Then the system is ACTIVE                  # features/steps/app_steps.py:67
    And the Energy mode remains unchanged      # features/steps/app_steps.py:97
    When I rotate the encoder RIGHT again      # features/steps/app_steps.py:47
    Then the Energy mode becomes the next mode # features/steps/app_steps.py:97

